---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Before a change is made
  accDescr: Managed policy must allow the command and remote writes, then the selected site's write switch must be on. Either can block the change. Tableau checks the user's permissions before applying it. Without a managed policy, the first gate adds no restriction.
  policy["1. Managed policy<br/>Allows this change?"]
  site["2. Site write access<br/>Enabled here?"]
  tableau["3. Tableau permissions<br/>User allowed?"]
  applied["Apply the change"]
  policy -->|Allowed| site
  policy -->|Denied| stopPolicy["Blocked"]
  site -->|On| tableau
  site -->|Off| stopSite["Blocked"]
  tableau -->|Allowed| applied
  tableau -->|Denied| stopTableau["Rejected"]
  stopPolicy ~~~ stopSite
  stopSite ~~~ stopTableau
  classDef stop fill:#f3e9df,stroke:#98745a,color:#684a34
  classDef done fill:#d3ed9e,stroke:#496641,color:#202720
  class stopPolicy,stopSite,stopTableau stop
  class applied done
